completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Steps to reproduce\n1. Take a .py file with a TODO line, e.g.:\n   #TODO: process lines...\n2. Optionally modify msg-template for pylint to make the problem more evident. E.g.:\n   `--msg-template={C}:{line:3d},{column:2d}: {obj}: {msg} ({symbol}, {msg_id})`\n3. Run pylint on the .py file above\n### Current behavior\n\nIn the pylint output, the W0511 warning (fixme) is formatted like this:\n`(fixme, W0511)O: process lines...`\nI.e., The beginning of the warning is overwritten by the end of the outputted line.\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe line should be formatted the same way as other warnings, i.e.:\n`W: 10, 0: : TODO: process lines... (fixme, W0511)`\n### pylint --version output\n\n```\nNo config file found, using default configuration\npylint 1.6.4,\nastroid 1.4.8\nPython 2.7.8 (default, Jul  2 2014, 19:48:49) [MSC v.1500 64 bit (AMD64)]\n```\n### Probable cause\n\nThe problem is probably caused by that W0511 doesn't strip off the end-of-line characters from the TODO line outputted in `{msg}`.\n","closed_by":{"login":"PCManticore","id":448166,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODE2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/448166?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore","html_url":"https://github.com/PCManticore","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"